                                "sense_id": "ac725c4d-34c3-3b62-a6eb-7e6cfd61c713",
                                "text": "While stooping over to fill his fan with unwinnowed grain, the buck, taking advantage of his position, came like a catapult against him, and sent him like a ball from a Paixhan gun, head foremost into the chaff."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a2da2cf-9661-4f1c-82b0-6c870c7fc41e",
                                "sense_id": "ac725c4d-34c3-3b62-a6eb-7e6cfd61c713",
                                "text": "A few miles away the loud Niagara of London runs swift, and the air vibrates with all the tumult of the strenuous life of man; but here the air is dead, unwinnowed by any clamorous wind, unshaken by any planetary motion."
                            }
                        ]
